# Classic white has no hash-pool skin power

Unmapped skins in getSkinPower use a stable string-hash into LOCAL_POWER_POOL. classic_white is intentionally unmapped and must stay in NO_POWER_SKIN_IDS so getSkinPower returns null (SkinPowerPanel already hides when !skinPower). Keep Siphon retired only; do not reintroduce it for this fix.

## Verification
- Verified: npm run lint && npm run build exit 0; classic_white in NO_POWER_SKIN_IDS returns null; SkinPowerPanel gates on !skinPower
- Failure pattern avoided: classic_white fell through getSkinPower hash fallback and showed a secret PowerSlot on starter dice
- Dead-end ruled out: Do not invent a SKIN_POWER_MAP entry for classic_white or edit powers.js Siphon/pool — return null via NO_POWER_SKIN_IDS
